      "body": "Hello @jiacheng-ye, thanks for tightening the padding-mask path for sequence parallelism.\r\n\r\nI checked the patch: it moves the `padding_mask` scatter in `GPTModel._preprocess()` out of the `pre_process` branch, so intermediate pipeline stages also receive an SP-local mask. That matches the failure mode where hidden states are already sequence-parallel local on every PP stage, but the mask was only scattered on the first stage.\r\n\r\nThis still needs the GPT/core owner path because it changes `GPTModel` behavior under SP+PP. I am assigned as current MCore oncall to confirm the required owner approval and move this out of `waiting-on-maintainers` once review/CI are satisfied.",
